WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.970
If you have Hepatitis
C, your liver

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.770
is inflamed because
you have been

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:20.630
infected with the
Hepatitis C virus.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.570
Your liver is the largest
organ inside your body

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:27.070
and performs many
important functions.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.620
The functional
parts of your liver

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.880
are called hepatic lobules.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.220
Your hepatic lobules filter
all of the blood in your body.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.110
As your blood
passes through them,

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:44.890
your hepatic lobules
breakdown harmful substances,

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:51.060
remove bacteria and
worn out blood cells,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.590
and form clotting factors
that control bleeding.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.340
After a meal, your
liver makes and stores

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:02.860
nutrients to provide your
body with energy when needed.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.120
Your liver also makes a
substance called bile.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.170
Your gall bladder
stores the bile

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.560
and releases it into
your small intestine

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.560
to help digest fats
in the food you eat.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.980
If you have Hepatitis
C, the virus

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.060
entered your body
when you were exposed

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.190
to the blood or
other body fluids

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.700
from a person infected
with the virus.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.790
This could have happened
from sharing a drug

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.630
syringe with an infected person.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.260
Other ways you may have been
exposed to the virus include:

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.650
having sex with someone
infected by the virus;

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:41.600
sharing personal hygiene items,
such as razors or toothbrushes,

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.590
used by an infected person;
direct contact with the blood

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:48.360
or body fluids of
an infected person;

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:54.300
or when a mother passes it
to her baby during birth.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.350
During the early, or acute
phase, of a Hepatitis C

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.900
infection, the Hepatitis
C virus enters your liver

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.230
and invades your liver cells.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.740
Once inside your
liver cells, the virus

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.490
begins to make copies of itself.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.020
During the copying
process, changes

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.550
called mutations
occur frequently

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.970
in the virus' genetic
material, leading

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.030
to new strains of the virus.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.240
In response to the
viral infection,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.780
your body sends immune
cells to attack both a virus

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.390
and the liver cells
infected with the virus.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:36.550
As a result, these liver cells
become inflamed and then die.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:41.400
Over time, scar tissue forms
around dead and infected liver cells.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.860
The scar tissue prevents your
liver from working properly.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.050
If you have a chronic
Hepatitis C infection,

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.110
your liver contains a large
amount of scar tissue,

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.610
called cirrhosis, which
limits blood flow and results

00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:00.450
in permanent shrinking and
hardening of your liver.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.220
A vaccine contains weakend,
or inactive, viruses

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.670
that train your immune system
to recognize and attack

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.970
certain viruses.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.630
However, frequent mutations
in the Hepatitis C virus

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.150
make it likely
that you will catch

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:19.050
a version of the virus not
contained in a vaccine.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.690
As a result, there is
no effective vaccine

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.430
for the Hepatitis C virus.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.000
If you have Hepatitis
C, your immune system

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.170
alone may destroy all
of the Hepatitis C virus

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.470
is in your body.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.200
However, most people
infected with the virus

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.250
develop chronic
Hepatitis C, a condition

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.130
in which your
immune system is not

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.030
able to destroy all of
the viruses in your body

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.070
after six months.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.180
If you have chronic Hepatitis
C and your immune system

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.290
can't get rid of the
virus completely,

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:54.950
your doctor may prescribe a
combination therapy consisting

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.730
of an anti-viral medication
called Ribavirin,

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.790
and injections of
Interferon, a medication that

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.830
strengthens your immune system.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:06.970
These drugs are most
effective against Hepatitis C

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.980
when taken together.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.680
If you have a severe case
of chronic Hepatitis C,

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.150
your doctor may recommend a
liver transplant operation.

